experiment: f3grid
  the question      §46 clause 4. Clause 3 showed a FIXED f3 target moves
                    the voice (5.1 SE, 9/9). Can f3 carry a CONDITIONAL
                    code -- two words differing only in f3, on an index
                    the creature derives itself?
  the design        ctxgrid's, axis swapped. Both arms hear identical
                    sessions; only whether the REWARDED target follows the
                    heard word differs. That isolates conditionality.
  the measure       which side of the pair's own f3 midline (2613.8 Hz) the
                    utterance landed on. Chance is 0.5 BY CONSTRUCTION and
                    no slot-to-word map is fitted on scored rows.
  render_f3_gain    1.00
  context_source    4

  instrument        f3grid   trial seed 000000000135d40d   18 creatures
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  arm           n     p3 (chance 0.500)    ctx_match (best-of-2, null > 0.5)
    conditional 18    0.786 +- 0.032        0.915   (early 0.930 -> late 0.884)
    random      18    0.544 +- 0.043        0.943   (early 0.953 -> late 0.914)

  CLAUSE 4a(i) -- IS THE INDEX LIVE? Measured, not read off the genome.
  `ctx_present_frac` 1.0000, `ctx_match` 0.9288 over all cells.
    -> live: the conditional arm has something to condition on

  CLAUSE 4a(ii) -- THE CONTROL. p3's chance is 0.500 by construction, so a
  random arm away from it means something is driving f3 UNCONDITIONALLY and
  the paired contrast is not purely about conditionality.
    random arm 0.544 +- 0.043, +0.044 from chance  -> at chance, as it must be

  CLAUSE 4b -- POWER, read BEFORE the contrast: SE on the paired excess
  0.0492 against the pre-registered ceiling 0.055  -> adequate

  CLAUSE 4c -- THE EXCESS, paired by seed and spanning the sign.
    conditional - random  +0.2427 +- 0.0492  (4.9 SE)   16/18 seeds positive
    -> F3 CARRIES A CONDITIONAL CODE. The third axis is nameable, the
       19-signal code space is cashable, and shipping render_f3_gain
       becomes a decision with evidence behind it

  AND COMPARE ctxgrid ON THE SAME MEASURE: its F1 excess was +0.126 and
  its F2 +0.082 at n=36. A null here against those is a statement about the
  AXIS, not about the design, because the design is the same one.
